PS5 HDMI: VRR test 15 (hdmi.vrr_test=1): + the complete stock pre-block message    [ps5-bazzite-deck, test only]

First VRR on a TV (Gilles, LG, 27 Oct, vrr-test10 with switches): with VRR
active, ignore-MSA, the GPU's Adaptive-Sync/FreeSync SDPs and the FreeSync
InfoFrame ("supported enabled active", through the bridge's InfoFrame slot)
the TV switched to FreeSync and showed the picture, while Sony's VSync
block was in its NORMAL mode. With the block in Sony's VRR mode the TV
reported 1 fps / no signal. Test 11 = test 10b with:
  - vrr_vsif on by default (FreeSync InfoFrame while VRR is active),
  - vrr_chip (new, default off): Sony's VRR block only on request,
  - the re-setup on VRR on/off keyed to the requested VRR state, so it
    still runs (for ignore-MSA) when the VRR block isn't used,
  - "ignore MSA" only while VRR is active (10b).
Opt-in with hdmi.vrr_test=1; not for a release.
Test 12 on top: Sony's VSync block at the position the stock 13.60 code calls it
(0x4b43cf in function 0x4b2570: after the PHY init, right before the additional
config), and the known part of the stock message written just before it
(7215=01 6207=80 621b=20; vrr_prep, default on). Both only in VRR mode (vrr_chip=1).
Test 13 on top: right after the VSync block, stock sends the HDMI Forum VSIF with
ALLM through the vendor-InfoFrame slot (0x72c0/0x72c4, 0x7203 bit 7, 0x7204 bit 7)
and sets 0x7214 bit 4 (function 0x607760, flag 0x353669c==1 in the VRR-on dump).
vrr_allm (default on), in VRR mode only.
Test 14 on top: logs once what the bridge advertises over DPCD (rev, dongle type,
branch ID/name/fw, MSA-ignore, Adaptive-Sync SDP caps, DFP/FRL caps) and raw DPCD
ranges 0x000, 0x080, 0x100, 0x2200, 0x2210, 0x3050, 0x500, to compare with what amdgpu's
HDMI-VRR-over-PCON path (CachyOS 7.2/hdmi, Tomasz Pakula) expects from a converter.
Test 15 on top: the pre-block message in full as hsgodd decoded it (7001|=03,
7061=5a 00, 7070=00 00, 7077=90 + 15-bit clock value, 7215=01, 6207=80, 621b=20).
Stock derives the 7077 value from a 24-bit number in the bridge's ICC reply divided
by 100; here the pixel clock in kHz / 100 stands in (vrr_7077 overrides, vrr_7061 too).
